1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,875
A tree is not a switch you flip.

2
00:00:02,825 --> 00:00:07,162
Plant it, and its crown is barely a metre and a half across.

3
00:00:07,162 --> 00:00:16,450
So CoolSpend grows each species on a Chapman-Richards curve — the forester's S-shape: slow at first, fast in the middle, easing off as it matures.

4
00:00:16,450 --> 00:00:23,525
A fast Tipuana fills its crown in twenty years; a slow Cercis takes forty — roughly twice as long.

5
00:00:23,525 --> 00:00:25,112
Now the money.

6
00:00:25,112 --> 00:00:27,687
Every euro is itemised.

7
00:00:27,687 --> 00:00:34,050
Two thousand two hundred to plant one tree — stock, pit, soil, guarding, labour.

8
00:00:34,050 --> 00:00:44,662
Then sixty euros a year to keep it alive, a figure we did not invent: it's Barcelona's own parks budget, twelve point six million divided by two hundred thousand trees.

9
00:00:44,662 --> 00:00:52,775
Run that over forty years, discounted at three and a half percent, and one tree costs about three thousand five hundred euros.

10
00:00:52,775 --> 00:00:55,562
Auditable, line by line.

